---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Optfall">
  <h1>Optfall</h1>

  <p>
    Legality that remembers, and rulings you can cite — a reference tool for
    Flesh and Blood.
  </p>

  <p>
    Optfall optimises for the one thing no incumbent optimises for: being right.
    Correct legality, correct rules text, correct rulings — each citable, each
    version-stamped, each with a permanent URL.
  </p>

  <p>
    No language model is involved in anything Optfall serves. Every answer is a
    parsed official document or a named human author, never generated prose — so
    a confidently wrong ruling is not a risk to manage but a thing the tool
    cannot do.
  </p>

  <h2>Status</h2>

  <!--
    Inline elements are kept on the same source line as the text around them.
    Astro compresses the built HTML and drops the whitespace at a line break
    that falls immediately before an inline tag, which silently welds words
    together in the output. Verified against dist/index.html.
  -->
  <p>
    <strong>Pre-Phase-0. Nothing is built yet.</strong> This page is the deployment target proving the pipeline works: a static build from <code>main</code>, a deploy preview on every pull request, and the compliance footer that ships before any product code does.
  </p>

  <p>
    The plan and the design language are written down and public: <a href="https://github.com/alxjrvs/optfall/blob/main/docs/PLAN.md">the phased build plan</a> and <a href="https://github.com/alxjrvs/optfall/blob/main/docs/DESIGN.md">the design pass</a>.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
